---
// The Google Play call-to-action, beside AppStoreButton on every page that offers the app (capabilities web-site,
// event-site). Renders NOTHING until the resolved deployment names the Play listing (`playStoreUrl`, empty until the
// listing is public): a closed-testing listing answers every other visitor with Play's "not found".
//
// The art is Google's official "Get it on Google Play" badge, unmodified — Google's brand terms require it, where
// the App Store button is our own. It ships with its clear space as transparent padding, so it is sized by that
// padded box (the badge body lands at the App Store button's height) and pulled in by a negative margin rather than
// cropped. Imported, so it is emitted same-origin under _astro/ (the self-containment invariant).
//
// On /join the island rewrites this link's href to carry the invite as the install referrer — only the one inside
// the event view, only for a valid invite (`src/lib/playReferrer.ts`). The markup itself never carries one: the page
// is byte-identical for every event. target=_blank for the same reason as the App Store button's.
import deployment from "../deployment.json";
import badge from "../assets/google-play-badge.png";
---

{deployment.playStoreUrl && (
  <a
    class="playstore"
    href={deployment.playStoreUrl}
    data-play-store={deployment.playStoreUrl}
    target="_blank"
    rel="noopener noreferrer"
    aria-label="Get SnapSync on Google Play (opens in a new tab)"
  >
    <img src={badge.src} width={badge.width} height={badge.height} alt="Get it on Google Play" />
  </a>
)}
